Paninda revision 004 — selected file, native Picker and conditional worksheet setup
Date: 2026-11-05 (UTC)
Branch: litmus_2
Base: 665efcf

CORRECTED REQUIREMENTS
- One selected Google Sheets file per device.
- Use Google's own picker, not a custom app-created-file list.
- Onboarding offers either an existing file or explicit creation of a named file.
- Required data worksheets live INSIDE that file, suffixed with " (Paninda)".
- Warn only when a selected file contains cell data AND is missing required app
  worksheets. Empty/compliant files do not receive a blanket warning.
- New onboarding choices/forms must share the existing gradient banner.
This revision supersedes log-rev003's blanket-warning/separate-file-only behavior.

IMPLEMENTATION
- Native Google Picker through AuthorizationClient PICKER_OAUTH_TRIGGER, CONSENT,
  drive.file ONLY, and setOptOutIncludingGrantedScopes(true). MIME restricted to
  Google Sheets; multi-file/folder selection disabled; exactly one returned ID
  required. Account identity uses a separate authorization request.
- Removed the custom workbook-list screen and appProperties-based discovery.
  Reads Drive metadata only for the selected file; verifies type/editability.
- Enable Google Picker API in the same Cloud project as Drive/Sheets. Existing
  Android OAuth package/SHA-1 registration is unchanged. No new API key, WebView,
  Web client ID, or broad Drive/Sheets scope is introduced.
- Gradient-banner FileSourceScreen asks Existing vs New. NewFileScreen asks for
  a file name and explicitly creates only when confirmed. Error retry clears the
  selected file and returns to this setup choice.
- Shared ConnectionPage keeps the Figma gradient/serif banner, scrolling body and
  fixed actions. Keyboard insets keep the new-file action accessible.
- Physical worksheet names:
    Meta (Paninda)
    Vendors (Paninda)
    Products (Paninda)
    Sales (Paninda)
    SaleItems (Paninda)
    StockMovements (Paninda)
  Internal mapper names remain unchanged, keeping existing domain fingerprints
  and the version-1 data contract stable.
- Inspect selected-file worksheet names and entered cells using FORMULA rendering
  so formulas returning empty strings still count as data. Missing worksheet names
  plus nonempty file data determine whether the warning is needed. Once all app
  worksheets exist, unrelated worksheet contents need not be scanned.
- Reinspect before initialization. If the file became nonempty/missing worksheets
  since selection, request the warning first. No initial mutation before approval.
- Proceed adds only missing app worksheets and initializes genuinely empty app
  worksheets at A1. Stage/validate existing app data in memory before modifying
  the file. Malformed app headers/data fail rather than being overwritten.
  Unrelated worksheets, including unsuffixed name collisions, are preserved.
- Recognize a complete valid legacy six-worksheet layout from the previous APK
  and rename those worksheets in place with the requested suffix. No record copy,
  deletion or reseeding. The current APK is needed afterward; earlier APKs expect
  the unsuffixed names.
- Local-first synchronization/conflict guards remain. An empty valid remote app
  dataset can receive retained local records even without a previous shared
  baseline; different nonempty copies still stop for review.
- Regular Sync Now does not silently recreate deleted app worksheets. It reports
  the missing schema and preserves local records for repair/reconnection.
- Updated page-specific strings and current setup/status/schema documentation.
  The Google logo placeholder and other pending business features are unchanged.

VERIFICATION
- All 16 maintained focused checks passed in the first build/test/lint pass.
  Three new data-policy tests cover warning conditions, protecting unrelated or
  malformed data, and recognizing valid legacy layouts. Existing sync test also
  covers uploading retained local records into newly initialized empty targets.
- Native Picker request/API symbols compile against the existing auth SDK 22.0.0.
  Google's official Android Picker documentation was checked:
  https://developers.google.com/workspace/drive/picker/guides/desktop-mobile-picker
- No maintained layout tests, screenshot baselines or size matrix added. Temporary
  direct-render inspection uses ignored work/ only.
- Final build/lint/render outcomes are appended after completion.

REMAINING ACCEPTANCE / LIMITS
- Google's actual Picker UI and account/file grant must be verified on a physical
  Play-services device after enabling Picker API. No live-device success claim
  is made from unit tests or preview renders.
- Existing single-writer/manual-sync limits remain: no conditional Sheets CAS,
  background worker, automatic merge or force-overwrite resolution.
- No arbitrary Excel/table import or automatic repair of malformed app data.
- Interrupted file creation may leave a file in Drive; review it before retrying.

FINAL CHECKS
- Final assembleDebug + lintDebug succeeded. Android lint: 0 errors. Remaining
  notices concern available dependency versions and optional toUri/KTX style.
- All 16 maintained regression checks passed again; the temporary direct-render
  harness also completed. Inspected source-choice, named new-file and compact
  large-text conditional-warning screens. Gradient/banner/actions are consistent;
  warning content and worksheet list scroll separately from the bottom actions.
- APK: app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk. No Google Drive upload or Git
  remote push requested for this correction turn; commit is local.
